# Build-context excludes. Without this, `COPY . .` drags the developer's
# host tree into the image.
#
# node_modules is the one that actually bites: it would land *on top of*
# the clean, lockfile-exact tree `npm ci` just installed, replacing it
# with whatever the host happens to have — silently, in a later layer
# than the one that was supposed to define it, and possibly built for a
# different platform. It also defeats the layer caching that copying the
# manifests separately exists to get.
node_modules
dist

# Never bake secrets into an image layer. Nothing in the image reads
# these — environment is passed in at run time (docker-compose.yml's
# `env_file:`), not baked in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
